# 9. PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS AND NUMERICAL MEASUREMENTS

This section is mandatory.

The simulator must calculate performance using actual generated signals.

### Input SNR

Calculate received input SNR using:

SNR_in = 10 log10(P_signal/P_noise)

Use the clean transmitted signal and actual added noise to determine the received channel SNR.

### Output SNR

Compare the recovered message with the original message.

SNR_out = 10 log10(P_reference/P_error)

Where:

- Reference is the original message.
- Error is the difference between the original and recovered signals.

Before calculating output SNR:

- Align signal delays.
- Remove DC offset.
- Correct receiver gain where appropriate.
- Use consistent measurement windows.
- Do not remove actual noise or nonlinear distortion through an artificial correction.

### Distortion

Calculate normalized mean squared error:

NMSE = Σ(x[n] - y[n])² / Σx[n]²

Also display normalized distortion percentage:

Distortion (%) = 100 × NMSE

Clearly identify this as normalized mean squared error-based distortion, not automatically as THD.

### Performance measurements table

Create an AM versus FM comparison table:

| Measurement | AM | FM |
| Input SNR | Measured | Measured |
| Output SNR | Measured | Measured |
| SNR improvement | Calculated | Calculated |
| Distortion (%) | Calculated | Calculated |
| Modulation index | Calculated | Calculated |
| Bandwidth | Calculated | Calculated |
| Receiver bandwidth | Displayed | Displayed |

All values must update whenever the simulation parameters change.

Do not hardcode example values into the results.

